{"step_index":744,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T14:58:07Z","thinking":"Initial testing confirms the `import_playbook` with the specified search variable successfully resolves `trp-wextp-be` hosts.\n\nNow, considering dynamic inventory population, the goal is to register all `trp-wextp-be*` and `trp-wextp-fe*` hosts using a specific method within the Ansible workflow. This will involve the use of a host-adding mechanism, likely on the `localhost` during a subsequent play.\n\n\nThe playbook will load a server pool, decode the data, and then filter to register backend and frontend hosts. Backend hosts matching the pattern `trp-wextp-be*` and the `WEXTP` group will be added to the `wextp_backends` group. The process will repeat to add frontend hosts to `wextp_frontends`.\n\n\nConsidering existing inventory usage, host registration should handle potential updates to existing groups. To ensure local CLI tools function correctly, discovered frontend and backend hosts need to be written into the inventory file.\n\nThe next stage will involve examining frontend server configurations. A Python script will scan Nginx configuration files to map upstreams and resolve backend targets for each server block.\n\n\nThe frontend configuration analysis will focus on resolving backend targets by parsing Nginx configuration and handling upstream definitions or direct host-port specifications. This process involves extracting backend server details and compiling domain route records.\n\nSubsequently, a backend check will be performed to determine the PHP version, ProxySQL configuration and status, and root directory for each domain on each backend server. This will use an embedded Python script to determine the PHP version via `php -v`, scan for all installed PHP CLI versions, and identify active PHP-FPM services.\n\n\nPHP-FPM will be examined to identify active pools and their corresponding ports by parsing configuration files and examining listening sockets. ProxySQL's status, version, configuration, and listening ports will be determined via command-line tools and configuration file analysis. Finally, a scan of the root directories will identify domains, along with their ownership, permissions, and index files.\n\n\nBackend server auditing focuses on verifying the existence of expected webroots for each domain by checking `/var/www/`.  This will involve extracting the branch name to compare the existence of backend server webroots.\n\nThe next step generates a detailed report for each backend server, including PHP, ProxySQL configuration summaries, and a listing of hosted webroots, along with a frontend-to-backend routing topology table.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -p 30 koby-bowser-ansible@172.30.230.97 'python3 -c \"\nimport glob, re, json\n\nupstreams = {}\n# Parse upstream definitions\nfor conf_path in glob.glob(\\\"/etc/nginx/omt/*.conf\\\") + glob.glob(\\\"/etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf\\\") + glob.glob(\\\"/etc/nginx/*.conf\\\"):\n    try:\n        with open(conf_path) as f:\n            content = f.read()\n        for m in re.finditer(r\\\"upstream\\s+([a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]+)\\s*\\{([^}]+)\\}\\\", content):\n            up_name = m.group(1)\n            body = m.group(2)\n            servers = []\n            for line in body.split(\\\"\\n\\\"):\n                line = line.strip()\n                if line.startswith(\\\"server \\\") and not line.startswith(\\\"#\\\"):\n                    parts = line.replace(\\\";\\\", \\\"\\\").split()\n                    if len(parts) >= 2:\n                        target = parts[1]\n                        host = target.split(\\\":\\\")[0]\n                        port = target.split(\\\":\\\")[1] if \\\":\\\" in target else \\\"80\\\"\n                        servers.append({\\\"target\\\": target, \\\"host\\\": host, \\\"port\\\": port})\n            if servers:\n                upstreams[up_name] = servers\n    except Exception as e:\n        pass\n\nprint(\\\"Upstreams found:\\\", len(upstreams))\nfor k, v in list(upstreams.items())[:5]:\n    print(k, \\\"->\\\", [s[\\\"target\\\"] for s in v])\n\"'","Cwd":"/home/koby/LINUX","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing upstream parser on fe1","toolSummary":"Test upstream parsing"}}]}
{"step_index":745,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T14:58:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-21T18:58:20+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-21T18:59:57+04:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n\r\n#####################################################################\r\n#                                                                   #\r\n# ~# Outremer Telecom #~                                            #\r\n#                                                                   #\r\n#      You are trying to login to an Outremer Telecom server.       #\r\n# Authorized uses only. All activity may be monitored and recorded. #\r\n#    Disconnect IMMEDIATELY if you are not an authorized user.      #\r\n#                                                                   #\r\n#####################################################################\r\n\r\nUpstreams found: 15\r\nSFRPROD74 -> ['trp-wextp-be6:17400', 'trp-wextp-be7:17400', 'trp-wextp-be8:17400', 'trp-wextp-be9:17400', 'trp-wextp-be10:17400']\r\nSFRPROD74-DEBUG -> ['trp-wextp-be10:17400']\r\nSFRBIZPROD74 -> ['trp-wextp-be6:17400']\r\nSFRBIZPROD74-NOREDIS -> ['trp-wextp-be6:37400']\r\nSFRDEV74 -> ['trp-wextp-be11:17400']\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":746,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T14:59:57Z","thinking":"Upstream configurations were successfully parsed, revealing fifteen distinct upstream definitions. The next logical step involves correlating these upstream definitions with the active server blocks within the `sites-enabled` configuration on the `fe1` environment. This should establish connections between the front-end servers and the defined backends.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -p 30 koby-bowser-ansible@172.30.230.97 'python3 -c \"\nimport glob, re, os\n\nroutes = []\nfor conf_path in glob.glob(\\\"/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*.conf\\\") + glob.glob(\\\"/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*\\\"):\n    if not os.path.isfile(conf_path):\n        continue\n    try:\n        with open(conf_path) as f:\n            content = f.read()\n        for block in re.split(r\\\"server\\s*\\{(?=\\s*(?:listen|server_name|include|root))\\\", content):\n            server_names = []\n            m_sn = re.findall(r\\\"server_name\\s+([^;]+);\\\", block)\n            for sn in m_sn:\n                server_names.extend([x.strip() for x in sn.split() if x.strip()])\n            \n            roots = re.findall(r\\\"root\\s+([^;]+);\\\", block)\n            doc_root = roots[0].strip() if roots else None\n            \n            passes = re.findall(r\\\"(?:fastcgi_pass|proxy_pass)\\s+([^;]+);\\\", block)\n            pass_targets = list(set([p.strip() for p in passes]))\n            \n            if server_names and pass_targets:\n                routes.append({\n                    \\\"conf\\\": os.path.basename(conf_path),\n                    \\\"domains\\\": server_names,\n                    \\\"root\\\": doc_root,\n                    \\\"targets\\\": pass_targets\n                })\n    except Exception as e:\n        pass\n\nprint(\\\"Routes found:\\\", len(routes))\nfor r in routes[:8]:\n    print(f\\\"{r[\\\"domains\\\"]} (root: {r[\\\"root\\\"]}) -> {r[\\\"targets\\\"]}\\\")\n\"'","Cwd":"/home/koby/LINUX","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing domain to upstream mapping on fe1","toolSummary":"Test domain mapping"}}]}
