{"step_index":754,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T15:02:56Z","thinking":"The system successfully mapped each domain to its corresponding root directory and upstream target. Observed mapping includes: `commande.sfrcaraibe.fr` to `/var/www/commande.sfrcaraibe.fr` to `SFRDEV82`, `espaceclient-lapostemobile.sfrcaraibe.fr` to `/var/www/espaceclient-lapostemobile.sfrcaraibe.fr` to `SFRDEV82`, and `espaceclient.sfrcaraibe.fr` to `/var/www/espaceclient.sfrcaraibe.fr` to `SFRPROD`. This looks complete.\n\n\nAdditional domain mappings have been established, covering services like business client portals, resiliation, rechargement, and SSO. The root directories and upstream targets have been systematically linked. There's a notable difference in the target for `espaceclientbusiness.sfrcaraibe.fr`, pointing to two possible targets. All other mappings seem to be singular.\n\n\nInitial investigation focuses on backend service (BE) configuration, specifically PHP versions, running PHP-FPM services and their listening ports. This involves verifying ProxySQL status and version, along with its configuration files and port usage. A directory scan of the web server's root will provide the final piece to understand the whole infrastructure.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -p 30 koby-bowser-ansible@172.30.230.118 'sudo python3 -c \"\nimport subprocess, os, re, glob, socket\n\nres = {}\n# Hostname & IP\nres[\\\"host\\\"] = socket.gethostname()\n\n# 1. PHP versions\nphp_cli = \\\"\\\"\ntry:\n    p = subprocess.run([\\\"php\\\", \\\"-v\\\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if p.returncode == 0:\n        php_cli = p.stdout.splitlines()[0].strip()\nexcept Exception:\n    php_cli = \\\"not installed\\\"\nres[\\\"php_cli\\\"] = php_cli\n\n# Active FPM services\nfpm_services = []\ntry:\n    p = subprocess.run([\\\"systemctl\\\", \\\"list-units\\\", \\\"--type=service\\\", \\\"php*\\\",